% Goal

Implement and maintain `brain/plan_bunch_activation.py` as the Per-plan activation records at plans/<slug>/bunches.json. THE DISJOINTNESS GATE LIVES HERE AND NOWHERE ELSE: an activation intersecting an already-enabled bunch is rejected naming the conflicting bunch_id and the shared track_ids, so the caller can render the conflict rather than a generic error. region is validated against the imported mix_order_brief.REGION_SLICES rather than a re-spelled copy. Activating an archived bunch is returned with a warning flag, not pruned. Every successful activate/deactivate appends EXACTLY ONE journal entry with rev_before/rev_after; a rejected activation appends NONE, because a 409 changed nothing. plans_activating(bunch_id) is a reverse lookup scanning plans/*/bunches.json so a library-level bunch edit or archive can journal into every plan it actually constrains; without it, archiving a bunch silently changes N plans with no trace in any of their journals.

% Product contract

- Preserve the exact public interface declared in `<pdd-interface>`.
- Treat the reviewed architecture description in this prompt as normative behavior.
- Keep plan identity, immutable track identity, revision guards, and non-destructive storage semantics intact across GUI, CLI, and agent callers.
- Preserve compatible behavior outside this module's stated responsibility; do not redesign unrelated mixing or playback logic.
- Reject malformed, stale, ambiguous, or unsafe writes explicitly instead of silently losing plan data.
- Keep the implementation deterministic where the contract describes deterministic behavior.
- Target Python 3.13+ for Python modules and baseline browser JavaScript without a bundler for browser modules.
- Inspect the current implementation, its declared dependency modules, and the focused tests before changing code. This is a brownfield source prompt: working, tested behavior not contradicted here remains part of the contract.

% Architecture detail

Per-plan activation records at plans/<slug>/bunches.json. THE DISJOINTNESS GATE LIVES HERE AND NOWHERE ELSE: an activation intersecting an already-enabled bunch is rejected naming the conflicting bunch_id and the shared track_ids, so the caller can render the conflict rather than a generic error. region is validated against the imported mix_order_brief.REGION_SLICES rather than a re-spelled copy. Activating an archived bunch is returned with a warning flag, not pruned. Every successful activate/deactivate appends EXACTLY ONE journal entry with rev_before/rev_after; a rejected activation appends NONE, because a 409 changed nothing. plans_activating(bunch_id) is a reverse lookup scanning plans/*/bunches.json so a library-level bunch edit or archive can journal into every plan it actually constrains; without it, archiving a bunch silently changes N plans with no trace in any of their journals.

